# Every check writes its evidence to a leading-underscore file in the repo root, and
# the list above grew one line at a time -- which means each new check leaves a stray
# artifact in `git status` until somebody notices. `_shared_tool.png` sat there for a
# day. These four rules cover the pattern; the named lines above are kept because
# deleting them would only churn the diff.
#
# .gitignore does not apply to files already tracked, so the `_dev_*.png` screenshots
# in the repo stay under version control regardless. The negation is here to say so
# out loud rather than leave it to be rediscovered.
_*.png
_*.jpg
_*.log
_*.err
!_dev_*.png
